<c74object name='lp.lana' category='Litter Power, Chaos'>

	<digest>Iterate a Latoocarfian attractor</digest>
	<description>lp.lana iterates a Latoocarfian map: x' = A(a y) + c C(a x), y' = B(b x) + d D(b y), with functions A to D (sin by default). Every bang outputs x (left) and y (middle). With unbounded functions (ident, sqr, sinh, cosh, exp), log or sqrt of negative values, or the poles of recip, cot and cotpi the point can become infinite or not a number; then it starts again at x0 y0 and the right outlet sends inf, -inf or nan (since 2026; before, inf or nan was sent from then on).</description>

	<metadatalist>
		<metadata name='author'>Peter Castine</metadata>
		<metadata name='tag'>Litter Power</metadata>
		<metadata name='tag'>Chaos</metadata>
	</metadatalist>

